    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardWelcomeTitle">Welcome</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardWelcomeHelp">A short setup for the display you play on, HDR, and refresh rate.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardWelcomeBody">Display Manager applies a Windows display profile when a game starts and restores the desktop when it stops. You can change everything later in Settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardDisplayTitle">Primary display for games</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardDisplayHelp">Choose which monitor should become primary when you launch a game, or keep the current Windows default.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardHdrTitle">HDR policy</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardHdrHelp">Default for every game. Per-game overrides in the game context menu always win.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardRefreshTitle">Refresh rate</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardRefreshHelp">Optional. Rates shown are those available on the chosen primary display at its current resolution.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardMigrationTitle">Clear Playnite native HDR activations?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardMigrationIntro">Playnite can turn HDR on for individual games with its own built-in option. If that stays on, Playnite and Display Manager may both try to restore HDR when a game closes. Clearing those activations lets Display Manager handle HDR alone. You can undo this later from Maintenance.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardMigrationCountFormat">{0} game(s) currently have Playnite's built-in HDR option turned on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardClearNative">Turn off Playnite's built-in HDR option on those games</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_SetupWizardMigrationHelp">If someone turns Playnite's built-in HDR option back on later, Display Manager turns it off again the next time that game launches (and notifies once).</sys:String>
